## Chapter 5 — System Analysis & Feasibility Study

### 5.1 Existing System Analysis

Most plant adoption programs operate through:
- **Paper-based applications** submitted at local municipal offices.
- **Static websites** listing plants without interactive features.
- **No feedback loop** — adopters have no mechanism to report plant health or receive community support.

### 5.2 Proposed System Advantages

| Aspect | Existing Systems | Green Guard |
|---|---|---|
| Application Process | Manual / Paper | Digital, role-based web forms |
| Plant Discovery | Offline lists | Geospatial map + search filters |
| Growth Tracking | None | Structured reports with photos & health metrics |
| Community | None | Social feed, likes, follows, comments |
| AI Features | None | Species identification via image upload |
| NGO Verification | Trust-based | Darpan ID + admin verification pipeline |
| Notifications | Email (if any) | Real-time in-app notifications |

### 5.3 Feasibility Study

#### 5.3.1 Technical Feasibility
- All technologies used (Node.js, Next.js, PostgreSQL, PostGIS) are mature, open-source, and well-documented.
- Supabase provides a managed infrastructure that eliminates the need for server administration.
- AI identification is offloaded to external APIs (PlantNet, Gemini), reducing computational requirements.

#### 5.3.2 Economic Feasibility
- The entire stack uses **free-tier services**: Supabase (free plan), Railway (free tier), Vercel (free tier).
- No hardware procurement is required — cloud-native deployment.
- Open-source libraries eliminate licensing costs.

#### 5.3.3 Operational Feasibility
- Intuitive, accessible UI designed for users of all technical backgrounds.
- Mobile-responsive design ensures usability across devices.
- Role-based dashboards reduce complexity by showing only relevant features to each user type.

### 5.4 Hardware & Software Requirements

#### Hardware Requirements
| Component | Specification |
|---|---|
| Processor | Intel Core i3 / AMD equivalent or higher |
| RAM | 4 GB minimum (8 GB recommended) |
| Disk Space | 500 MB for source code + dependencies |
| Network | Internet connection required |

#### Software Requirements
| Software | Version |
|---|---|
| Operating System | Windows 10/11, macOS, or Linux |
| Node.js | v18.0 or higher |
| npm | v9.0 or higher |
| Web Browser | Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Edge 90+ |
| Code Editor | VS Code (recommended) |
| Database | Supabase (managed PostgreSQL 15) |
| Version Control | Git 2.30+ |

